===Etymology===
From {{inh|wym|gmh|nesse|alt=neʒʒe}}, from {{inh|wym|goh|nazī|t=wetness}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|Nässe}}

===Noun===
{{wym-noun|f|pl=nessa}}

# rainy weather
# [[wetness]]

====Related terms====
* {{l|wym|nessa}}

===Etymology===
From ''finesse'', by clipping and reinterpreting the suffix ''-ness'' as a verb. 

====Verb====
'''ness''' (third-person singular simple present '''nesses''', present participle '''nessing''', simple past and past participle '''nessed''')

# *(informal, neologism)* To transform a rage-typed or otherwise  emotionally charged message into a collaborative, goal-oriented communication before sending, typically with the aid of an AI writing tool such as ChatGPT.

=====Usage notes=====
Often applied in digital communication contexts like emails, texts, and social media posts where emotionally reactive drafts are refined using AI tools to achieve a productive outcome through tone adjustment and goal alignment.

=====Examples=====
* *The email was so infuriating she had to ness her reply before sending it.*  
* *I was about to send a savage text but decided to ness it with ChatGPT first.*  
* *Hang on, let me ness this before I get myself fired.*  
* *That post made me so mad I rage typed a comment, then nessed it into something actually helpful.*

=====Synonyms=====
* finesse (contextual)  
* rephrase  
* diplomacize (humorous, informal)

=====Related terms=====
* finesse  
* edit  
* rephrase  

